From a076e81b0700005bd99b38db0562b535c431062f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 17:16:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 39/43] test(chexc): joins and meets, and the erasure of
 clauses at the symbol level

'join_meet.cj' is the text's own pair of examples -- the join unions the lists, the meet of two
unrelated ones leaves a requirement-free parameter -- and 'covered_meet.cj' pins the comparable
case, where the meet keeps the narrower entry. The meet had no test at all until now.

'abi/erasure_symbols.cj' compiles the same package twice, with every clause and with none, and
requires the two symbol tables to be identical; 'erasure_clause_twin.cj' runs the same shapes.
Erasure was argued from the architecture and never pinned, which the review noted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
